# Inputs to build.py, one per line: <sha256>  <name under data/source/>  <origin>
#
# origin is one of
#   a URL                 fetched by fetch-sources.sh (to a .part file, renamed
#                         only once its sha256 matches)
#   git:<commit>:<path>   a blob from this repository's history, by full commit
#   stream:<URL>          a mosaic too large to download, which build.py streams
#                         through HTTP range requests (usgs_remote). Its digest
#                         is the sha256 of the per-chunk sha256s of the pixel
#                         data, in chunk order, checked as it streams.
#
# build.py re-checks every file it reads against this list. When an upstream
# file is replaced on purpose, update its line here and the affected
# outputs.sha256 entries together.
